<title>UK: BRITISH BEET TEST SHOWS 77 GRAMS SUGAR PER ROOT.</title>
<headline>BRITISH BEET TEST SHOWS 77 GRAMS SUGAR PER ROOT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar beet test carried out Monday August 11, issued by British Sugar Plc.</p>
<p>			  2nd TEST   2nd 1996   5YR AVG</p>
<p> SUGAR GRAMS/ROOT	  77	  57	 65.3</p>
<p> SUGAR PCT		15.77     15.11	15.36</p>
<p> ROOT GRAMS/WT	    495	 379	  423</p>
<p>&quot;Analysis of the second field samples indicates that following good establishment and favourable weather conditions, the prospects for this year's beet crop are good,&quot; British Sugar said. &quot;If these conditions continue, it would indicate a better than average national crop. However, this is only the second sample and there is a long way to go,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
